**Optimizing mathematical functions**

I'm tackling the optimization of the gradient single ratio with the fugacities being a function of the exponential of beta, but there's some complexity with the PhiRsign in a single determinant scenario. It seems tricky to optimize negative R without it affecting other determinants. Since we're starting with positive values, crossing into negative W might be more likely. I’ll have to ensure the structure is well-organized as I work through the analytic ratio with real coefficients.
